  "goodToKnow": "Der Bräutigam is the bridegroom; die Braut is the bride, and das Brautpaar the couple. German wedding traditions include the Polterabend, a party before the wedding where guests smash crockery for luck and the couple clears it up together, and sawing a log (Baumstamm sägen) after the ceremony. The legally valid wedding is at the Standesamt. Plural: die Bräutigame."
